    "highlights": "Text transformations like `text-transform: uppercase` are used for technical and micro UI text (LatteraMonoLL) and headings (STORE LOCATOR). Lowercase is exclusively used to distinctively brand product names such as `ear ( 3a )` and `phone ( 4a )`.",
    "insights": [
      "The Nothing brand identity heavily leverages typography, notably using the distinctive dot-matrix `Ndot` font for hero typography, logos, and product names (often styled in lowercase or uppercase depending on context).",
      "`NType82` is deployed as a high-contrast utilitarian sans-serif for body copy and secondary headings, providing modern structural clarity, and unusually lightweight weights (100) are utilized to create an airy visual balance against the technical aesthetics.",
      "`LatteraMonoLL`, a monospace typeface, is strictly allocated for UI components, form fields, callouts, and functional labels, reinforcing a technical, code-like, and brutalist aesthetic."
    ]
